usr/lib/grub/x86_64-efi/crypto.module	grub_reset_gcry_hwf_x86_64_efi	vzeroupper runs only when hw_features has the AVX bit: grub-core/lib/x86_64/efi/hwfeatures-gcry.c:210 tests it; :201-202 set it only if enable_avx() returns true, which needs CPUID.01H:ECX bits 26 and 28 (:163-164) and OSXSAVE bit 27 (:179-180). Compiled code: testb $0x2 at 0x12af, je at 0x12b2, vzeroupper at 0x12d1. qemu64 CPUID.01H:ECX AVX=0 and OSXSAVE=0 (lfs13-logs/ch8close/cpuid.qemu64.txt), so the bit is never set there. Cryptodisk path not run (static gate evidence)	haiku-agent/2026-11-07
